      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How requests run",
      "items": [
        "Desktop streams audio and visual input through Gemini Live.",
        "Channels run a separate Gemini loop; replies return through the originating transport.",
        "Arrows show requests and calls. Results return to the caller."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Capabilities and storage",
      "items": [
        "The SDK loader registers extension tools, hooks, commands and skills; each host builds its own dispatch.",
        "Channel transcripts use per-agent SQLite. Memory still includes separate SQLite and Markdown stores.",
        "CLI starts cron handlers when declarations exist. LanceDB is an optional local memory extension."
      ]
    },
